{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/concurrencyandcancellation"]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Concurrency & Cancellation"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The guarantees "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" makes about overlapping, cancelled, and reset calls."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStatePreviewError","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Pagination"],"anchor":"Modeling-state","title":"Modeling state"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and built under Swift 6 strict concurrency. Every "},{"code":"load","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadNextPage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" call is "},{"code":"async","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which raises three questions the moment a screen does more than one of them: what happens if a second call starts before the first finishes? How do you stop one early? And how do you force a store back to a known state outside of any of them? This article covers all three."}]},{"anchor":"Overlapping-calls-only-ever-apply-the-latest-result","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overlapping calls only ever apply the latest result"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing extra is needed to handle a screen firing off a second call before an earlier one has finished — a fast double-tap on Retry, or a new search query arriving before the previous one resolved:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await store.load { try await api.fetchArticle(id: 1) } \/\/ slow — still in flight","await store.load { try await api.fetchArticle(id: 2) } \/\/ fast — resolves first"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Internally, every call stamps itself with a token before running "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and only applies its result — "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", or the "},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" mapping "},{"code":"loadCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" do — if that token is still the most recently started one by the time "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" resolves. In the example above, article 1’s slower fetch resolving "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"after"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" article 2’s result is already showing never overwrites it; its result is silently dropped. "},{"code":"refresh(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" follows the same rule: it only clears once the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"newest"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" in-flight refresh finishes, not whichever overlapping one happens to resolve first. "},{"code":"loadNextPage(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"code":"isLoadingNextPage","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" follows it too."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need to call "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for this to hold — it’s automatic. Reach for "},{"code":"cancel()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" when you additionally want to stop the older call’s work from running at all, not just prevent its result from landing."}]},{"anchor":"Cancelling-explicitly","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Cancelling explicitly"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" to stop whatever call is currently running, without waiting for it to resolve:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["store.cancel() \/\/ e.g. from onDisappear, or right before firing off a newer query"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (and "},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") are left exactly as they were — cancelling never surfaces a "},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the way letting "},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" itself fail would. This applies uniformly, including to "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadWithRetry(maxAttempts:backoff:_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" cancelled mid-backoff: it stops retrying and leaves "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" untouched, just like every other call. If nothing is in flight, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel()"},{"text":" does nothing.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Cancelling-automatically","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Cancelling automatically"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A store also cancels whatever it was still tracking when it’s deallocated, as a last-resort safety net — you don’t need to call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel()"},{"text":" from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"text":" yourself. In practice this rarely has anything to do: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"text":"\/etc. already ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" their own work to completion before returning, so by the time a store can actually be deallocated, there’s normally nothing left in flight to cancel. It exists to guard against that assumption changing later, for free.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Resetting-outside-of-a-load","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Resetting outside of a load"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/reset(to:)","isActive":true},{"text":" snaps a store back to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":" (or any state you give it) without going through ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"text":" at all — useful for a full sign-out flow, where whatever the store was showing or fetching no longer applies to the next signed-in user:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func signOut() {","    session.clear()","    articlesStore.reset() \/\/ back to .loading, as if freshly created","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel()"},{"text":", it stops whatever operation is currently in flight; unlike ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cancel()"},{"text":", it also immediately replaces ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"text":" and clears ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"text":", so a screen bound to the store reflects the reset right away instead of waiting for a cancelled operation to unwind.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/cancel()":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Cancels whatever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ref